> 
> When you are wielding a lance, you can hit directly adjacent squares
> as with any other wielded weapon.

This only really works while riding. When on foot, using the lance on
adjacent monsters counts as "bashing" - it's treated as though you
were hitting the beasts with a non-weapon item (foot-melee using a
lance is, i think, equivalent to foot-melee using a crystal ball as
weapon).

When you attack adjacent monsters with a lance while riding, you will
"joust" them, and this does a load of extra damage. Since jousting
eventually breaks a lance, it's still better to use the sword as
standard weapon and only swap in the lance on occasion.

> > 3. Lugh is always less than well-pleased. I am not killing things that
> > don't hit me first, and the pony is not dead. I try not to hit fleeing
> > monsters, waht else could it be?
> 
> Lugh is a bitch.  Convert as soon as possible, I can recommend Brigit.

Uh, that's a joke, right? There's no special code making Lugh lousy -
he's as good/bad as any other lawful deity. I think it's just the
knight who has a tendency to run into trouble a bit too frequently in
the early game - no resistances, no superb killing power, no food,
less-than-incredible hitpoint gain.

Definitely _don't_ convert "as soon as possible", because this will
render your game unwinnable. Generally, never convert unless you know
what the consequences are and either don't care - or don't need to
care anymore.

